    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe repo derives read-only `Owner` response fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`) by declaring them in the OpenAPI schema and letting MapStruct auto-map them from matching getters on the `Owner` entity. I followed that same convention:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (which drives generation of the `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived getter:\n   ```java\n   public String getContactPreference() {\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n       return hasEmail ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n   MapStruct auto-maps the DTO field from this getter (no mapper change needed). The email presence check mirrors the existing `getMembershipLevel()` logic for consistency.\n\nThe acceptance tests confirm `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `contactPreference` = `PHONE` for an owner with no email and `EMAIL` once an email is present.\n\nI kept `contactPreference` as a plain string (rather than an OpenAPI `enum`) specifically so the generated DTO field is a `String` and MapStruct maps it cleanly from the `String` getter, avoiding a generated enum type and the String\u2192enum conversion that would require.",
